Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts it as a message to a specified Slack channel using the Slack API:

```javascript
function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  const token = 'YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN'; // Replace with your actual Slack API token
  const url = `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage?token=${token}&channel=${channel}`;

  fetch(url, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text: text
    })
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => console.log('Message posted to Slack:', data))
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting message to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postMessageToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Replace `'YOUR_SLACK_API_TOKEN'` with your actual Slack API token and `'#general'` with the desired channel name.

