response:
Your MATLAB code is a good starting point for finding unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2. Here's an optimized version that can handle a large amount of text:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(text1, text2)
    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));

    % Create a set of unique words in Text1
    uniqueWords1 = unique(words1);

    % Find unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2
    uniqueWords = uniqueWords1(~ismember(uniqueWords1, words2));
end
```

This function first converts both texts to lowercase and splits them into words. It then creates a set of unique words in Text1 using the `unique` function. Finally, it finds the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 by checking if each word in Text1 is a member of Text2 using the `ismember` function.

To use this function, simply call it with your two text files as arguments:

```matlab
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt');
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt');
uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(text1, text2);
disp(uniqueWords);
```

This will print out the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2.

