It seems like the issue is with the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header being set to * (wildcard), which allows requests from any origin. When this happens, the browser may not send the Authorization header with the request, as it assumes that the server will allow access regardless of the authentication credentials.

To resolve this issue, you can either:

1. Set the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header to a specific domain or IP address that you trust, rather than using a wildcard (*). This will ensure that only requests from trusted sources can include the Authorization header.
2. Use a pre-flight request (OPTIONS method) to check if the server supports CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) and if so, to obtain the necessary CORS headers. You can then use these headers in subsequent requests to include the Authorization header.

Here's an example of how you can use a pre-flight request in JavaScript:
```javascript
const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
xhr.open('OPTIONS', 'https://example.com/api/endpoint', true);
xhr.setRequestHeader('Access-Control-Request-Method', 'GET');
xhr.setRequestHeader('Access-Control-Request-Headers', 'Authorization');
xhr.send();

xhr.onload = function() {
  const response = JSON.parse(this.responseText);
  const accessControlHeaders = response.headers['Access-Control-Allow-Headers'];

  // Check if the Authorization header is allowed
  if (accessControlHeaders && accessControlHeaders.includes('Authorization')) {
    // Include the Authorization header in subsequent requests
    const authToken = 'your_auth_token';
    const authorizationHeader = `Bearer ${authToken}`;
    xhr.setRequestHeader('Authorization', authorizationHeader);

    // Make the actual request
    xhr.open('GET', 'https://example.com/api/endpoint', true);
    xhr.send();
  } else {
    console.log('Authorization header is not allowed.');
  }
};
```
This example sends a pre-flight request to the server to check if the Authorization header is allowed. If it is, the script includes the Authorization header in the subsequent

