To leverage the Accord.NET library in C# to train and implement the Naive Bayes algorithm for text classification, follow these steps:

1. Install the Accord.NET NuGet package.
2. Create a new C# console application.
3. Import the necessary namespaces:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Accord.MachineLearning;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Text;
using Accord.Math;
```

4. Load the dataset of labeled sentences. You can use a CSV file or any other suitable format.

```csharp
string dataPath = @"path\to\your\dataset.csv";
var dataset = TextClassification.ReadDataset(dataPath);
```

5. Split the dataset into training and testing sets.

```csharp
var split = dataset.Split(0.8);
var trainingData = split[0];
var testingData = split[1];
```

6. Create a Naive Bayes classifier and fit it on the training data.

```csharp
var naiveBayes = new NaiveBayes();
naiveBayes.Fit(trainingData);
```

7. Use the trained classifier to predict the labels of new observations.

```csharp
var prediction = naiveBayes.Predict(testingData);
```

8. Compute the conditional probabilities of each word in a sentence given each category.

```csharp
var wordProbabilities = naiveBayes.GetWordProbabilities();
```

9. Utilize these probabilities to classify a new sentence into one of the three categories.

```csharp
string newSentence = "The sports game was exciting";
var classification = naiveBayes.Classify(newSentence);
```

10. Output the predicted label.

```csharp
Console.WriteLine($"Predicted label: {classification}");
```

